This directory defines the https://docs.kalico.gg website. The
site is hosted using "github pages". The
.github/workflows/cd-docs.yaml tool uses mkdocs (
https://www.mkdocs.org/ ) to automatically convert the markdown files
in the docs/ directory to html. In addition to the files in this
directory, the docs/CNAME file also controls the website generation.

To test deploy the main site locally one can use commands
similar to the following:

```bash
cd docs/_kalico/ # if you were in the repo root
uv venv
uv sync
uv run mkdocs serve
```

The Simplified Chinese site is built with a separate configuration
(`mkdocs.zh.yml`) and published under `/i18n/simple-chinese/`. The
deployment workflow (`cd-docs.yaml`) builds both sites, then copies the
shared assets (`img/`, `logo/`, `prints/`, `resources/`, `_kalico/css/`)
into the Chinese site output. To build it locally:

```bash
cd docs/_kalico/
uv run mkdocs build -f mkdocs.zh.yml
cp -r ../img ../logo ../prints ../resources site/i18n/simple-chinese/
mkdir -p site/i18n/simple-chinese/_kalico/css
cp ../_kalico/css/extra.css site/i18n/simple-chinese/_kalico/css/extra.css
```
